"""Fictional example sentences for the "Ready-to-use rewrite" shown next to every detected claim.

The template (in app.py) says what a company still has to fill in. The EXAMPLE shows the same sentence completed
for an INVENTED company, so a non-expert can see what a good answer looks like. The example has to feel relevant:
a bank should not be shown a bottle of water, nor a supermarket a power plant. So the example is written per
claim topic/type (`key`) and adapted to a sector profile (`profile`) chosen from the scanned company's sector.

Every example is a format string. A profile supplies the words that make it fit the sector ({co}, {site},
{prod} ...); a profile can also replace a whole example (OVERRIDES) where the general wording would not make sense
for that sector (for example "per bottle" for a bank). Everything is invented: no real company or figure.
"""

